# PowerOfTwoMaxHeap

A max heap in which every parent node has 2^`childExponent` children. The exponent is passed to the constructor. An exponent of 0 gives a chain, 1 gives a binary heap, 2 gives four children per node, and so on up to 30.

Because the branching factor is a power of two, parent and child positions are computed with shifts instead of division:

```
parent(i)     = (i - 1) >>> childExponent
firstChild(i) = i * 2^childExponent + 1
```

The heap is stored in a flat array with no per-node objects. `insert` and `popMax` move values through a hole instead of swapping them, so each element is written once per level.

